From: At30c <PabloAtsoc9993@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] m21s: restore ordered TEEgris startup after node fix

The asynchronous property actions allowed post-fs to continue while TZTS and
its ACSD connection were not established.  Normal-boot pstore consequently
showed a ready base tzdaemon but no persistent tzts_daemon, while Keymaster
and Keystore2 remained blocked.  The original Samsung sequence is safe again
after explicitly preparing all three TEEgris device nodes.

Run the complete TEEgris chain synchronously in post-fs, wait for both daemon
readiness properties, and only then restart the legacy Keymaster bridge and
Keystore2.  This preserves Samsung's required ordering without the former
device-node permission deadlock.

--- a/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
+++ b/etc/init/teegris_v3.rc
@@ -14,15 +14,13 @@ on post-fs
     chmod 0660 /dev/tziwshmem
     start tz_service
     start tz_msg_recv
-
-on property:vendor.tzdaemon=Ready
+    wait_for_prop vendor.tzdaemon Ready
     setprop vendor.TEEGRIS.loaded true
     write /proc/iccc_ready 1
     start tzts_service
-
-on property:vendor.tzts_daemon=Ready
+    wait_for_prop vendor.tzts_daemon Ready
     restart vendor.keymaster-4-0
     restart keystore2
 
 on post-fs-data
 # TEEGRIS service
